{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13120-me-and-my-angeleater","id":13120,"title":"Me and my angeleater","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-17T19:15:10-08:00","id":13120,"title":"Me and my angeleater","content":"Well I don't know if it's occurred to anyone else but in gmc, you can have ghosts and spirits who have the numina to eat angels.<br /> <br /> Not only do they make great weapons against angels, a generous GM might even consider their conversion of angelic essence to ghostly or spiritual essence might even give out aether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T15:01:56-08:00","id":13640,"title":"","content":"Why would the GM be generous? Its angels are being eaten, after all! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> More seriously: given that ghosts and spirits exist in a different kind of Twilight than angels do, how would this work in the first place? Wouldn\u2019t they both have to Manifest before the meal could commence? <br /> <br /> Finally, you make an interesting observation: since there are now different flavors of Essence (e.g., spiritual, ghostly, and angelic), it makes sense that Aether is the byproduct of the use of the specific kind of Essence associated with angels, and no others. Put another way, \u201cEssence\u201d isn\u2019t one thing, any more than \u201cpower stat\u201d is: it\u2019s a collective term for the fuel stats used by ephemeral beings. Implication: when werewolves speak of \u201cEssence\u201d, they\u2019re usually speaking of <i>spiritual</i> Essence; and they\u2019re no more interested in hunting ghosts or angels than, say, a changeling is interested in collecting Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T15:16:31-08:00","id":13652,"title":"","content":"Given that Sin-Eaters can gain plasm from eating ghosts and Vampires can (according to Book of the Dead) learn to get Vitae from Ghostly Essence, but probably not from Spiritual Essence, I'd agree. Plus, there's the fact that (from what I've read, at least) a Geist is born from a ghost eating a spirit or vice versa (since spirits and ghosts can share the same Twilight so long as they're on the same side of the Gauntlet), so Spirit and Ghost Essences are close to one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T00:31:27-08:00","id":13831,"title":"","content":"Actually DW, you're wrong, book of the dead reveals that werewolves can eat ghosts for essence just like any human and the fact that the idigam can manipulate both spirits and ghosts using their essence shaping abilities means that any differences between the forms of essence aren't that great,<br /> <br /> As for how &quot;essence thief&quot; works, I would assume like you that it requires manifestation of some sort, but I didn't write GMC so I don't know what they had in mind.<br /> <br /> But you apparently skipped over the word conversion, since the very word conversion requires by definition the assumption that the types of essence aren't exactly the same, one doesn't convert an apple into an apple. A spirit or ghost with essence thief eats some essence from an angel, option one is that the spirit or ghost converts the angelic essence into spiritual or ghostly essence in their pseudo stomach. Whenever angelic essence is used aether is produced, so why wouldn't the essence thief using angelic essence to make the correct form of essence count as use?<br /> <br /> Option two is that the angelic essence is still angelic essence, in which case obviously when the essence thief uses that stolen essence aether would be produced, because aether is produced whenever angelic essence is used whether by an angel or anything else.<br /> <br /> Hmm since essence thief is just a numina, you could even use that numina to justify crossovers. Why wouldn't a demon love a mage with an essence thief fetish or a sin-eater with an essence thief fetter?<br /> <br /> Now for the record I wouldn't argue with any ST who thinks that's just too much of a benefit, but I don't see any reason other than game balance why it wouldn't work that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T06:52:40-08:00","id":13996,"title":"","content":"Obviously, this is up to the ST, but I believe that the GMC rules about Ghosts, Spirits and Angels supersedes both Book of the Dead and Book of Spirits info.<br /> <br /> I believe GMC introduced the idea that there were three different types of essence (one for each ephemeral being) and that these beings do not exist in the same &quot;frequency&quot; while in a Twilight state. Hence why Angels are such a big deal in GMC, as they are the only things that can break this rule given adequate power by the GM. I believe the point is that Spirits and Ghosts only run into each other in rare circumstances now. As opposed to the previous fluff that had them exist side by side in Twilight.<br /> <br /> Now, this is not to say that the Numina does not work as you mentioned. It does convert different essence types (or at least that was also my reading of it), so it does theoretically let a Ghost or Spirit feed off an Angel. Though I would be inclined to split the Numina into a &quot;greater&quot; and &quot;lesser&quot; version. The &quot;lesser&quot; version allowing the same type of essence to be stolen. While the &quot;greater&quot; version would allow for essence conversion from other types. The first I would make reasonably uncommon among Ghosts and Spirits. The second I would limit to some very select Spirits and Angels. <br /> <br /> This is just my take on things of course. I just like the idea that Angels should be a little more powerful then Ghosts or Spirits, particularly for a Demon game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T08:50:41-08:00","id":14082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13120-me-and-my-angeleater?p=13996#post13996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, this is up to the ST, but I believe that the GMC rules about Ghosts, Spirits and Angels supersedes both Book of the Dead and Book of Spirits info.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13120-me-and-my-angeleater?p=13996#post13996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe GMC introduced the idea that there were three different types of essence (one for each ephemeral being) and that these beings do not exist in the same &quot;frequency&quot; while in a Twilight state. Hence why Angels are such a big deal in GMC, as they are the only things that can break this rule given adequate power by the GM. I believe the point is that Spirits and Ghosts only run into each other in rare circumstances now. As opposed to the previous fluff that had them exist side by side in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Close. GMC introduced the idea that there are multiple types of ephemera (the substance that Twilight beings are composed of), and it doesn\u2019t explicitly say anything about Essence coming in similar types. However, the latter is an obvious and logical extrapolation of the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T09:36:23-08:00","id":14107,"title":"","content":"Yeah I don't remember any talk about different &quot;types&quot; of essence, only that different Ephemera only interact with the twilight of their Ephemera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T09:43:18-08:00","id":14117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13120-me-and-my-angeleater?p=13996#post13996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the point is that Spirits and Ghosts only run into each other in rare circumstances now. As opposed to the previous fluff that had them exist side by side in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou must've been living under the assumption of a much thinner Gauntlet, then, because it was my understanding that while they both existed in a state of Twilight when in the real world, spirits had to actually cross over from the Shadow in order to be in Twilight in our world, and that wasn't exactly the easiest thing to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T09:46:25-08:00","id":14126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13120-me-and-my-angeleater?p=14107#post14107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I don't remember any talk about different &quot;types&quot; of essence, only that different Ephemera only interact with the twilight of their Ephemera.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the entire premise of spirits being changed by the nature of what they eat on a macroscopic scale; the ghost caveat of the Spirit Manipulation Essence Shaping power in Wolfsbane makes a note of what their Essence resonates with (their anchors) and Shadows of the U.K.'s Twilight to Twilight section demonstrates two examples of what happens when spirits consume ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T10:39:56-08:00","id":14160,"title":"","content":"I wonder how much of that material is still valid post-GMC. As Eldagusto pointed out, ephemeral beings being able to interact with each other in Twilight is a pre-GMC thing; if it still exists at all post-GMC, it probably requires special powers designed to facilitate cross-ephemera interactions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T11:11:45-08:00","id":14189,"title":"","content":"Except that Geist's...er... Geists were, if not in the books then on the old forums (I know I read it <i>somewhere</i>), specifically stated to be weird Ghost-Spirit Hybrids, thus explaining why Mages couldn't mess with them without using both the Death and Spirit Arcana. Geists are both and neither, and while they may be rare, they're not <i>overwhelmingly</i> so, which is what you seem to be suggesting, DW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T13:30:21-08:00","id":14254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13120-me-and-my-angeleater?p=14126#post14126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the entire premise of spirits being changed by the nature of what they eat on a macroscopic scale; the ghost caveat of the Spirit Manipulation Essence Shaping power in Wolfsbane makes a note of what their Essence resonates with (their anchors) and Shadows of the U.K.'s Twilight to Twilight section demonstrates two examples of what happens when spirits consume ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to the GMC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T13:31:55-08:00","id":14257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13120-me-and-my-angeleater?p=14189#post14189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that Geist's...er... Geists were, if not in the books then on the old forums (I know I read it <i>somewhere</i>), specifically stated to be weird Ghost-Spirit Hybrids, thus explaining why Mages couldn't mess with them without using both the Death and Spirit Arcana. Geists are both and neither, and while they may be rare, they're not <i>overwhelmingly</i> so, which is what you seem to be suggesting, DW.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Geists are actually rare. Its just most folks that don't plumb the Depths of the Underworld rarely run into them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T14:28:21-08:00","id":14293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13120-me-and-my-angeleater?p=14189#post14189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that Geist's...er... Geists were, if not in the books then on the old forums (I know I read it <i>somewhere</i>), specifically stated to be weird Ghost-Spirit Hybrids</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not &quot;specifically stated to be&quot; ghost-spirit hybrids. That's a theory pitched in the books with no confirmation one way or the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> thus explaining why Mages couldn't mess with them without using both the Death and Spirit Arcana. </div> </div> </div>Summon Chthonian uses Death, Spirit and Prime, despite the entities in question only needing Death to affect, and Astral entities only take Mind to summon despite allowing them to possess people requiring the use of Spirit spells with equal parts Mind. The Arcana are not a good metric for what the more obscure beings are beyond the broadest strokes.<br /> <br /> Besides which, the double Arcana requirements smacks of parallel development hitches, since geister are already harder to affect than ghosts thanks to the Not Quite Ghosts quality tacking a -2 penalty on to attempts to affect them like ghosts. (And this connection may be illusory, but I'd like to note that -2 is the same penalty Book of Spirits puts to attempts to use human-affecting supernatural powers on spirits.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Geists are both and neither, and while they may be rare, they're not <i>overwhelmingly</i> so, which is what you seem to be suggesting, DW. </div> </div> </div>I'm fond of suggesting that geister represent one way ghosts <i>become</i> the Underworld's <i>equivalent</i> of spirits \u2014 they know the place inside and out down to the negotiation of both physical and social labyrinths that one encounters when trying to navigate the Great Below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T15:32:04-08:00","id":14330,"title":"","content":"You just took the words out of my mouth. To clarify, I\u2019m not trying to imply that geists (the plural spelling used in the book) are rare; I\u2019m just stating facts: GMC has revised the rules for Twilight in a way that makes interaction between ghosts and spirits (or between either and angels) highly unlikely. <br /> <br /> As Satchel pointed out, there are spirit-like entities in the Underworld. As far back as <b>Second Sight</b>, the description of the Voodoo Tradition of thaumaturges made it clear that there are godlike entities that counted as ghost-like rather than spirit-like for the purpose of Thaumaturgy\u2019s rituals, but are not ghosts. <b>Summoners</b> described Cthonians. <b>Geist</b> described the Kerberoi. You don\u2019t have to go to the spirit world to find entities that embody concepts related to Death; and it\u2019s far more likely IMHO that the text in <b>Geist</b> that suggests the possibility that geists are created when ghosts consume personifications of death is referring to chthonians (which I use as a catch-all term for any ephemeral entity that\u2019s made of the same kind of ephemera as a ghost but is not a ghost). <br /> <br /> And to be clear: the box that talks about geists and spirits phrases it as \u201cdoesn\u2019t that sound a lot like spirits? Why yes, it does. If you want them to <i>be</i> spirits, you can.\u201d <br /> <br /> Finally, <b>Geist</b> has an unusually troubled history in terms of its development, and several of its developers have said that if they had it to do over again, they\u2019d do a number of things differently. One in particular said that he doesn\u2019t like the \u201cghosts consuming spirits\u201d theory and doesn\u2019t use it. <br /> <br /> All of this is not to say that you can\u2019t have angel-eaters; but it\u2019s not as easy to manage as it would have been prior to GMC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T18:25:55-08:00","id":14431,"title":"","content":"Right... different types of ephemera for each entity. Which the logical extrapolation of different types of essence for each. <br /> <br /> Like I said earlier. This means that its not bog standard for Ghost and Spirits to interact anymore. As previously any Spirit that breached the gauntlet into a twilight state was on the same &quot;frequency&quot; (had the same type of ephemera) as ghosts. Hence a lot of Death spirits eating Ghosts in the old fluff. <br /> <br /> Now if the ST (and for the sake of this argument us as well) decides in his/her chronicle/campaign that GMC rules and metaphysics over rules anything from previous books e.g. Book of the Dead, Book of Spirits, Wolfsbane, Shadows of the UK and Second Sight. Then the norm is that Ghosts and Spirits cannot interact in Twilight by default. If the ST wanted he/she could go with the interpretation that these being cannot even really perceive each other. Which I kinda like the idea of myself.<br /> <br /> Angel's likewise would exist in their own &quot;frequency&quot; of Twilight. However, given that they can be custom modded by the GM to fulfill the task it needs its possible they could get given Numina that let them perceive and interact with Ghosts and Spirits. Considering a lot of the tasks Psychopomps seem to get is &quot;move that entity back into its native realm/dump it in another realm&quot; it would make sense that these Numina exist.<br /> <br /> I don't see these Numina being a common naturally occurring power in Ghosts or Spirits though. Maybe powerful or unique examples of each that gain a lot of rank and influence in spheres that might relate to the other e.g. a powerful Death spirit. I would say they were exceedingly rare outside custom Angels basically.<br /> <br /> Now this is not to say that Ghosts and Spirits don't EVER bump into each other anymore. I am sure the Underworld has verges to the Shadow and that the Shadow has Avernian Gates in it that a Spirit might &quot;trip&quot; through when they open. So the idea that the two beings can meet, fight, eat each other and mingle (and if you want too produce a Geist) is still possible. Its just a much, much rarer occurrence then previously. Which as an ST I have no problem with. Mainly because it makes Angels more unique from other ephemeral beings and it makes being able to see &quot;Twilight&quot; a more variable ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T19:38:13-08:00","id":14467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13120-me-and-my-angeleater?p=14431#post14431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said earlier. This means that its not bog standard for Ghost and Spirits to interact anymore. As previously any Spirit that breached the gauntlet into a twilight state was on the same &quot;frequency&quot; (had the same type of ephemera) as ghosts. Hence a lot of Death spirits eating Ghosts in the old fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. You're thinking of chthonians, who presumably still do the whole anaconda-esque eat-and-digest thing with ghosts.<br /> <br /> The main spirit-examples of Ghost-Eater show up in Shadows of the U.K., where consumption of ghosts is a particularly common ban among bird-spirits, the spirits of graveyards have a ten-year cycle of Watchers tied into their ghost-eating, and Saucy Jack's attendant brood of madness-murder-and-fear ate him when he died to become something that looks an awful lot like a geist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now this is not to say that Ghosts and Spirits don't EVER bump into each other anymore. I am sure the Underworld has verges to the Shadow and that the Shadow has Avernian Gates in it that a Spirit might &quot;trip&quot; through when they open. So the idea that the two beings can meet, fight, eat each other and mingle (and if you want too produce a Geist) is still possible. </div> </div> </div>Avernian Gates from the Shadow don't have keys and from context seem to be perpetually open, which I'm going to guess was intentional to leave the hybridization theory open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T16:56:00-08:00","id":14974,"title":"","content":"Guys, guys:<br /> <br /> There's a Numina - in GMC - that explicitly enables one type of Ephemeral Entity to interact with another type. Presumably specifically to prevent this sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T17:13:52-08:00","id":14986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13120-me-and-my-angeleater?p=14974#post14974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, guys:<br /> <br /> There's a Numina - in GMC - that explicitly enables one type of Ephemeral Entity to interact with another type. Presumably specifically to prevent this sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, dude:<br /> <br /> Essence Thief is literally just Ghost Eater reskinned to work on more things. Like, legit, the mechanics are identical. Book of the Dead gave Ghost Eater to ghosts to replicate the Essence-thievery spirits got up to among themselves for ghosts and now ghosts don't need a Numen to do that and the Numen that draws direct mechanical descent from it now has an effect that's more broadly useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-20-2013, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T18:32:27-08:00","id":15031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13120-me-and-my-angeleater?p=14986#post14986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, dude:<br /> <br /> Essence Thief is literally just Ghost Eater reskinned to work on more things. Like, legit, the mechanics are identical. Book of the Dead gave Ghost Eater to ghosts to replicate the Essence-thievery spirits got up to among themselves for ghosts and now ghosts don't need a Numen to do that and the Numen that draws direct mechanical descent from it now has an effect that's more broadly useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I've been going through the GMC ephemeral entities rules again. Basically each type of entity can only interact with their own type of entity by default (plus the &quot;geography&quot; of the Twilight formed by &quot;ghost buildings/landmarks&quot;). Laws of physics are a bit screwy in that state so getting around is quicker then in the material state (particularly if you are the sort of being that &quot;should&quot; be able to fly e.g. bird spirit/winged angel). As part of an ephemeral entities base nature they can attempt to steal essence from entities of the same type via an attack.<br /> <br /> That's it according to GMC. So by default ghost interact with ghosts, spirits with spirits and angels with angels. People who project into Twilight interact with non of these as they have no true ephemeral form.<br /> <br /> Now taking a few Numina (such as essence thief) allows the entity in question to spend essense (a single point) to be able to attack other ephemeral entities to attempt to steal their essense. Allowing for your Death Spirit that eats Ghosts and Angel that beats up Spirits and throws them back into the Shadow.<br /> <br /> However, no type of ephemeral entity starts off with this Numina by default. So how common it is in a given game is up the ST, basically. In my games I'd been inclined to make it a rare Numina primarily the province of Angels given the task of sorting out Ghosts or Spirits for the GM.<br /> <br /> So to answer the question posed in this thread. Theoretically a Demon could make friends with/form and alliance/manipulate a Spirit or Ghost that had the Essence Thief and this &quot;friendly&quot; ephemeral entity could then be of some use to the Demon if he/she ever had a confrontation with an Angel.<br /> <br /> However the question has to be if that MORE useful (given the work required to even get such an allie/pawn) then the Exploit that shuts down GM related beings in an area (Reality Reinforcement) or the Essence Drain Demonic Form Technology. The latter in perticular lets you drain Angelic Essence or Demonic Aether, and with the ST's approval could be used to drain Ghosts, Spirits or even other major splats such as Werewolves and Mages.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, I seem to have got my wires crossed somewhere with the GMC rules to do with Rank. Is it the case that a higher Ranked entity does Agg damage with its attacks to entities of a lower rank then it? I'm sure I read that at some point but can't find the passage that mentions it in the book.<br /> <br /> Edit = Likewise, while it never directly mentions different &quot;types&quot; of essence, the GMC does hint at the idea. Since each of the three entities have unique was of getting Essence back. They all have some generic ways, but the fact that ONLY Ghosts get essence from being remembered and ONLY Spirits get essence from Loci and that ONLY Angels get essence from Infrastructure is kinda telling I think. Certainly it has some thematic basis if an ST wants to roll with that idea. In such a case I would guess the Essence Thief Numina would &quot;convert&quot; the essence type stolen to one that the entity in question could use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 11-20-2013, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}